; BlindSkills.inix -- how this database opens, and how its table is heard.
;
; FREE LESSONS IN BLINDNESS SKILLS, from the Blind Skills directory by Jamal
; Mazrui: videos and podcast episodes that teach cane travel, guiding, braille,
; cooking, dressing, labeling, money, crafts and more, in twelve skill groups.
; Each lesson has its skill (the task it teaches), summary, source, presenter,
; series, year, medium, and where known its length, publisher page and transcript.
;
; PLAY ONE. Play Stream (Alt+Shift+P) plays the lesson itself in the Homer
; Player: an audio episode directly, a video on YouTube or Vimeo through yt-dlp.
; Mark several (Space) and Alt+Shift+P plays them all, as a play list. None come
; marked, so the first Alt+Shift+P plays the lesson you are on. The whole
; directory is also a play list, BlindSkills.m3u, beside its web page, for
; FileDir's Homer Player. Control+Enter on source_url opens the publisher's page,
; and on transcript_url opens the transcript.
;
; FIND ONE. The row speaks title, medium and source: what it is, whether you will
; hear audio or a video, and who made it. The rows are grouped by category, as
; the directory groups them, so lessons on one skill sit together. category,
; skill, source, series, audience, medium and structured_discovery are pick
; lists, so filtering on one offers its values; each category comes with the
; directory's own definition. tags repeat the group, skill and source, so
; Keywords (Control+K) finds a lesson by any of them.
;
; QUERIES AND REPORTS. Skill-Index lists every lesson by the task it teaches;
; Audio-Lessons the episodes made to be heard; With-Transcripts those with a
; transcript to read in braille or by speech; Structured-Discovery those about the
; method or made where it is taught. The practice_list report writes up the
; marked lessons; skills_handbook writes up every lesson, grouped by skill group,
; to keep or print.
;
; scripts\makeBlindSkills in DbDo's development folder rebuilds this file from
; the directory.
;
; [Database] decides which table the window starts on. [Table:<n>] decides which
; fields the row speaks, in what order, and how the rows are sorted. DbDo writes
; these keys back whenever you change the columns, the sort or the filter.

[Database]

InitialTable = lessons

[Table:lessons]

SelectFields = title, medium, source
; OrderFields, 14 October 2026: by skill group, as the directory reads, then by title; skills do not age as software does.
OrderFields = category, title
WhereFilter =

[Table:lookups]

SelectFields = fld, val
OrderFields = fld, ordinal
WhereFilter =

[Table:maps]

SelectFields = kind, prime1, prime2
OrderFields = kind, prime1
WhereFilter =
